<BaseLayout title="Projects — Jonas El Gammal" description="Bright Interface GmbH, Graphsmith, and independent technology projects by Jonas El Gammal."><header class="page-head"><div class="shell"><span class="eyebrow">Beyond the research portfolio</span><h1>Projects</h1><p>Companies and technical experiments that turn data, automation, and machine intelligence into usable systems.</p></div></header>
<article class="prose project company" id="bright-interface"><span class="status">Company · Co-founder, Managing Director & CTO</span><img class="company__logo" src="/assets/icons/bright-interface.svg" alt="Bright Interface logo"/><p class="lead">An integrated data and automation platform for medical practices in Germany.</p><p>Bright Interface GmbH is building the connective layer that many practices currently lack: a system that assimilates fragmented operational data and turns it into coordinated services for patients, medical teams, and practice management. The aim is not to automate clinical judgement, but to make the surrounding workflows more accessible, reliable, and efficient.</p><div class="outcomes"><section><span>01</span><h3>For patients</h3><p>Online booking, voice-assisted routine interactions, reminders, delay notifications, self check-in, and proactive invitations for vaccinations and check-ups.</p></section><section><span>02</span><h3>For medical teams</h3><p>Less administrative overhead through better scheduling, documentation support, task tracking, and connected workflows.</p></section><section><span>03</span><h3>For practices</h3><p>Operational visibility across appointment duration, room utilisation, capacity, and management KPIs through a unified dashboard.</p></section></div><h3>My role</h3><p>As co-founder, Managing Director and CTO, I lead product and technical strategy, system architecture, engineering quality, data integration, applied AI, and technical delivery.</p></article>
<article class="prose project graphsmith"><span class="status">Active experiment</span><h2>Graphsmith</h2><p class="lead">An AI-native planning and execution system built around typed graph programs.</p><img src="/assets/img/graphsmith_pipeline.svg" alt="Graphsmith planning, compilation and execution pipeline"/><p>Language models are good at semantic intent but unreliable at emitting large executable structures directly. Graphsmith separates these jobs: a model proposes a typed intermediate plan, while deterministic machinery compiles, validates, repairs, executes and traces the graph.</p><h3>Current direction</h3><p>The project explores guarded execution, loop lowering, local repair, reusable skills, trace-derived promotion signals, and trust-aware remote reuse. Its central bet is that inspectable graph structure gives models—and people—a better substrate for understanding and repairing programs than opaque one-shot generation.</p><p><a class="button button--solid" href="https://github.com/jonaselgammal/Graphsmith">View Graphsmith on GitHub</a></p></article></BaseLayout>
<style>.project{padding-top:2.5rem}.project+.project{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:3rem}.project .lead{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.35rem;color:var(--ink)}.graphsmith>img{background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);margin:2rem auto;max-width:600px;width:100%}.company__logo{background:transparent;margin:1.5rem 0 2rem;max-width:520px;width:min(100%,520px)}.outcomes{display:grid;gap:1px;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);margin:2rem 0;background:var(--line);border:1px solid var(--line)}.outcomes section{background:var(--paper);padding:1.3rem}.outcomes span{color:var(--signal);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.65rem}.outcomes h3{margin:.65rem 0 .5rem}.outcomes p{font-size:.88rem;margin:0}@media(max-width:760px){.outcomes{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
